1
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,720
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:10,530
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,500
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,370
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:21,370
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:35,260
Can't we go any faster?

7
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:36,330
No.

8
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:38,660
Any faster and it'll be too hard on Griffith.

9
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,770
They're catching up.

10
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:05,500
Feel no shame about shape

11
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,420
Weather changes their phrase

12
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:11,170
Even mother will show you another way

13
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:13,550
So put your glasses on

14
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:15,630
Nothing will be wrong

15
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

16
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,680
It's up to you

17
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:23,310
The first words should be found

18
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:26,940
Whatever holds you back

19
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:28,310
I...

20
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:29,440
...can...

21
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,610
I can get it off

22
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:32,610
Tell me what...

23
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:33,610
Tell me what...

24
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:35,440
Tell me what you want

25
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:36,530
I don't know why...

26
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:37,530
Don't know why...

27
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,530
Don't know why you're afraid

28
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,700
Tell me what...

29
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:41,660
Tell me what...

30
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:43,330
Tell me what you'd say

31
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,660
I don't know why...

32
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:45,750
Don't know why...

33
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:46,540
Too late...

34
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,170
It's too late

35
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:57,090
Eve of the Feast

36
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:05,810
First unit, continue pursuit!

37
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:07,430
Second unit, follow my lead!

38
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:08,350
To the valley!

39
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,070
At this rate, they'll catch up
with us any second!

40
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,120
We have no choice!

41
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,450
Should we attack?

42
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:26,000
No, we'll make it!

43
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,800
We thought we'd welcome
you with bows and arrows.

44
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,930
I'm counting on you to look after Griffith.

45
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:42,800
We'll take good care of him, big sister.

46
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:46,640
We're going to annihilate our
pursuers here, once and for all!

47
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:49,730
Bastards!

48
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:50,810
Charge!

49
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:08,250
What happened?

50
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:18,590
Stop right there!

51
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:27,390
Bastard!

52
00:03:27,390 --> 00:03:28,470
Don't move.

53
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,730
Now slowly put your
weapons down and surrender!

54
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:41,450
I'm sure you thought you could revive
your group with this man's return, but...

55
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:44,030
Stop it!

56
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:44,870
Behold!

57
00:03:48,870 --> 00:03:51,410
This man will never fight again!

58
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:55,170
He will never ride a horse,
nor hold a sword again...

59
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:58,800
He can't even stand on his own two feet!

60
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:03,760
You've made a grave mistake.

61
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:07,640
There is not a single shred
of hope left for any of you.

62
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:15,370
Hey, it's not true, is it?

63
00:05:15,370 --> 00:05:19,080
What that bastard said
was a load of bullshit, right?

64
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:25,420
Screw you, guys! I'll ask him myself.

65
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,720
You can't do that.

66
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:28,090
What do you mean?

67
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:30,930
Griffith can't give you an answer.

68
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:35,310
You've got to be kidding.

69
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:38,770
So his throat got a little dry living in prison?

70
00:05:38,770 --> 00:05:40,110
And that's why...

71
00:05:52,030 --> 00:05:56,080
What the hell!

72
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,460
This is supposed to be our new beginning!

73
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:02,210
We were going to make a fresh start
after we rescued Griffith, right?

74
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:07,420
For a year we've lived like squirming
bugs, losing half our men...

75
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:12,600
But after believing for so long that all
we had to do was get Griffith back...

76
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:15,270
This is what we get?

77
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:24,070
You know, I had a feeling it would
turn out like this, seriously...

78
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:26,280
But...

79
00:06:27,650 --> 00:06:29,410
But even so...

80
00:06:44,090 --> 00:06:45,300
What are we going to do?

81
00:06:47,050 --> 00:06:50,090
What on earth are we going to do now?

82
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,390
It's not like we've
been totally wiped out.

83
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:58,020
And we have you, Casca...

84
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:00,230
There's no Band of
the Hawk without Griffith.

85
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:03,020
You all should know that.

86
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:04,860
Yeah, but if that's the...

87
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:08,400
Casca's pushed herself
harder than anyone else.

88
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,200
So stop making unreasonable demands.

89
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,320
Yeah, but...

90
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,910
What about us...

91
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,160
Please give me...

92
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:19,040
...some time.

93
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:23,080
We still have time until the others join us.

94
00:07:23,830 --> 00:07:26,300
Let me think this over until then.

95
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,680
Hey, wait up!

96
00:07:39,730 --> 00:07:41,190
What is there to think over?

97
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:42,810
What are you planning?

98
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:44,100
You're not thinking of continuing...

99
00:07:44,610 --> 00:07:45,520
What were you...

100
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:47,520
...about to say back there?

101
00:07:49,030 --> 00:07:51,900
That if it's a battle of your own choosing...

102
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,490
...then you'd better settle it yourself.

103
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,240
That shows... how strong you are.

104
00:07:58,290 --> 00:08:02,500
Because for us, even if we started
something, we can't always finish it.

105
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:08,630
Can you really look Griffith
in the eye now and say that?

106
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,720
We're all weak.

107
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:17,260
So we cling to others and to dreams...

108
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:22,560
We cling to kind words of comfort...
and even to harsh words of rebuke.

109
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:30,860
All I've wanted was someone
to cling to... To be by my side.

110
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:46,040
I'll go check on Griffith.

111
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:57,390
Griffith, let's change your bandages.

112
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,060
Whether it's a good dream or a bad dream...

113
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:04,520
No one feels good when
woken up in the middle of one...

114
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:09,610
So are you going back to traveling
and perfecting your combat skills?

115
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,610
I guess. And you?

116
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,650
Well...

117
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:19,280
Perhaps I'll bring along the guys that
are left and form a band of thieves.

118
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:23,160
That way, I'm sure we can
at least take care of Griffith...

119
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,250
I'll come too.

120
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:27,170
You already left us once, remember?

121
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,960
You have no obligation
to stick with us any longer.

122
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:30,840
But...

123
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:32,670
...you do?

124
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:37,510
Sure, I'm still one
of the Band of the Hawk.

125
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,510
But you're different.

126
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:42,680
You've already begun
fighting your own battles.

127
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,270
Leave behind those
who can no longer stand up.

128
00:09:46,270 --> 00:09:48,060
That's the law
of the battlefield, isn't it?

129
00:09:49,310 --> 00:09:51,060
But that aside...

130
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:54,360
You better be sure to take
Casca with you this time.

131
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:59,110
She's too much of a straight arrow
to be leading a pack of thieves.

132
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,410
A thief with a conscience? No thanks...

133
00:10:02,410 --> 00:10:03,120
Not for me!

134
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,870
I mean it.

135
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:06,710
Take her with you,
even if you have to drag her.

136
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:08,210
Commander!

137
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:09,370
Commander Guts!

138
00:10:10,330 --> 00:10:14,300
Hey, are you planning to leave
us again without saying a word?

139
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:17,590
If you go, please let us go with you!

140
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:20,260
We've all talked it over and agree...

141
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,890
Not one of us wishes otherwise.

142
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,260
You guys...

143
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,970
As long as you're there...

144
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:27,730
We'll make it through, somehow.

145
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:28,390
Commander!

146
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:30,480
Please take us with you...

147
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,230
Commander...

148
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:32,190
Please, Commander...

149
00:10:38,490 --> 00:10:39,700
Perhaps...

150
00:10:40,030 --> 00:10:42,120
...this has been my home all along.

151
00:10:44,830 --> 00:10:48,000
I didn't realize it until this very moment...

152
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:52,290
Everything I wanted back then
is right here in front of me now.

153
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:54,800
Why?

154
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:58,550
Why do I never realize
what I have until it is lost?

155
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:18,280
Griffith's hands...

156
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:21,490
I never realized how small they were...

157
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,780
He tried to grasp everything
with these two hands...

158
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:29,910
Just by placing this hand on my shoulder...

159
00:11:30,410 --> 00:11:32,580
...he always made my fears subside...

160
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:36,250
He saved me time after time...

161
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:42,550
Now I must do the same for him.

162
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,140
Oh...

163
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,730
Um...

164
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:53,310
Um, I...

165
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,110
Sorry...

166
00:11:56,110 --> 00:11:58,020
I'll go get more bandages...

167
00:12:00,490 --> 00:12:02,240
Griffith, st...

168
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,430
Hey...

169
00:12:31,930 --> 00:12:32,890
How's Griffith?

170
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:35,310
He just fell asleep...

171
00:12:35,650 --> 00:12:37,230
Something wrong?

172
00:12:38,690 --> 00:12:40,400
No, nothing's wrong...

173
00:12:42,110 --> 00:12:44,280
What the hell's going on?

174
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,780
No, really, it's nothing!

175
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,780
So you're crying over nothing?

176
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:50,450
Did something happen to Griffith?

177
00:12:50,450 --> 00:12:51,410
No, stop!

178
00:12:52,370 --> 00:12:53,580
It's not that!

179
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:54,750
Hey...

180
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,590
I'm sorry...

181
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:00,500
I can't go...

182
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:01,710
What?

183
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:05,130
I-I can't go with you...

184
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,800
Griffith...

185
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,470
...he's so small...

186
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:12,640
...and he's trembling so much...

187
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:16,440
When he used to be
so proud and dignified...

188
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:19,110
I can't leave him behind...

189
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:22,110
I can't leave him like that...

190
00:13:24,570 --> 00:13:25,360
I'm sorry...

191
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,320
I'll stay...

192
00:13:28,490 --> 00:13:29,070
...as well.

193
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:33,660
You're through clinging
to other people's dreams...

194
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:36,870
You have your own battles
to fight, remember?

195
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,920
You have to go...

196
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:44,880
If you're Griffith's true friend...

197
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,420
...you have to leave.

198
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,260
Even without me, you have to go.

199
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:18,250
Why are you trembling
with fear in a place like this?

200
00:14:44,070 --> 00:14:45,030
Let's go...

201
00:14:48,570 --> 00:14:50,410
I still want to play some more!

202
00:14:54,530 --> 00:14:56,490
The sun hasn't set yet.

203
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:18,100
Griffith!

204
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,810
But how?

205
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,190
Did he hear us?

206
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:23,310
I'll go after him!

207
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:26,230
Go tell the others!

208
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:45,380
I've rested too long...

209
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,380
It's time to go...

210
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,630
It's not over yet...

211
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:55,800
As long as that cobblestone path
keeps leading me on...

212
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:05,480
Griffith...

213
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:07,230
Griffith...

214
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:11,360
Supper's ready.

215
00:16:11,650 --> 00:16:13,410
Oh, were you asleep?

216
00:16:13,410 --> 00:16:14,530
Sorry...

217
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:17,330
...but we need to get some air in here...

218
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:18,790
Where am I?

219
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:19,870
What?

220
00:16:19,870 --> 00:16:22,120
Is there something on my face?

221
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:25,420
You were dreaming about
the old days again, weren't you?

222
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:28,040
A dream...

223
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:31,170
I see. That's all it was.

224
00:16:31,170 --> 00:16:35,470
It's been a while since any
of the guys came by to see us.

225
00:16:35,470 --> 00:16:37,140
I wonder what they're all up to?

226
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:42,350
I wonder if that guy's still waving
his big sword around somewhere?

227
00:16:44,230 --> 00:16:49,570
The past feels like nothing
more than a dream now.

228
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,780
Hey! Guts!

229
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,200
Leave Pippin alone!

230
00:16:54,530 --> 00:16:55,860
Go wash your hands!

231
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:57,240
Yes, Mother!

232
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,540
Many things happened...

233
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:03,710
But they're all just distant memories now.

234
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:07,420
I think I'm much more suited to this lifestyle...

235
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:10,840
My life with you and
our boy, just the three of us...

236
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:19,850
This kind of peaceful life is not so bad.

237
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:49,940
It's called a behelit, the Egg of the King.

238
00:18:50,650 --> 00:18:53,150
The owner of
this necklace is destined to hold...

239
00:18:53,150 --> 00:18:56,110
...the world in his hands,
in exchange for his flesh and blood.

240
00:18:57,690 --> 00:19:00,860
In exchange for his flesh and blood?

241
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,740
Griffith...

242
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:08,160
...was it really me who drove you to this?

243
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:11,290
Am I responsible
for what has become of you?

244
00:19:11,830 --> 00:19:13,130
What should I do?

245
00:19:13,130 --> 00:19:14,500
What do you want me to do?

246
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,710
What can I do for you now?

247
00:19:20,430 --> 00:19:21,590
What's that?

248
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:22,930
What the...

249
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,430
A solar eclipse...

250
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,660
Griffith!

251
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:58,630
Stay away!

252
00:20:01,380 --> 00:20:02,680
Guts!

253
00:20:23,110 --> 00:20:24,910
What the hell is that?

254
00:20:24,910 --> 00:20:25,570
Soldiers?

255
00:20:25,870 --> 00:20:28,080
Can it be the Midland army?

256
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:29,620
I don't know...

257
00:20:30,750 --> 00:20:32,580
I don't know what it is...

258
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,210
But it's ominous...

259
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:38,090
Griffith!

260
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,090
Don't come near me!

261
00:20:40,090 --> 00:20:42,050
Griffith!

262
00:20:42,050 --> 00:20:43,090
Don't come near me!

263
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,430
If you touch me now...

264
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:49,560
If you grasp my shoulder now...

265
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,310
I'll never again...

266
00:20:54,890 --> 00:20:57,020
I'll never again... you.

267
00:21:04,610 --> 00:21:05,660
Griffith.

268
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

269
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

270
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

271
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

272
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

273
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

274
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

275
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

276
